  "method": "Candidate overlay. Unclipped new feature and grass render at 4x with four WORLD pixels of overscan on every side (416x352). Feature/bank edges use analytic signed-distance AA, 0.25 world-pixel ramp; distances round to 1e-9 world px for reciprocal half-alpha stability. Existing alpha-aware Lanczos3 reduces the UNMASKED overscan 416x352 -\u003e 208x176. Crop 4-world-pixel margins AFTER filtering to 384x320 and 192x160, then apply complementary hard half-open polygon ownership at final pixel centers. No per-sprite polygon-edge AA; a future complete-map compositor may AA its outer boundary once. Each port has \u003e=8 straight world pixels and extends beyond cutout by outer radius+4; cubic connectors flatten at 64 steps; junctions merge by minimum distance. No legacy footprint or pixels. Optional road markings=dashed: 0.9-world-pixel light centre dashes and 0.6-world-pixel continuous edge lines one world pixel inside each pavement edge, eight-world-pixel nominal dash length and twelve-world-pixel nominal period; eight-world-pixel port phases are reciprocal, curved interiors fit the phase, junction centres remain unmarked. Narrow dusty shoulders blend the earth material with RGB(177,168,145) at weight.35. Marked-road verge only: add 0.65*E*(0.65*sin(3A+2B)+0.35*sin(7A-5B)) world pixels to the configured shoulder, where E=S((minimum polygon edge distance-8)/8), A=2pi(x/142+y/80), B=2pi(x/142-y/80). Pavement width and road markings are unchanged; the first eight world pixels at every port retain fixed shoulder width.",
  "original_image_inputs": [
    {
      "generation_recipe": "art/recipes/terrain/shore-reference-v2/water.json",
      "path": "build/pulse-study/dos-04/PARTS/SSSEA083.png",
