    }
  ],
  "original_image_inputs_scope": "Semantic visual references used to paint the current masters or their fixture ground. Originals remain reference-only and are not bundled as runtime PNGs; source masters are newly painted. Unit sprite planes retain their existing independent artwork provenance.",
  "ownership": "Binary final-pixel polygon ownership: cross(edge,point)\u003e0; on an edge include dy\u003c0 or dy==0 \u0026\u0026 dx\u003e0 (top-left rule), exclude the reciprocal edge. Ground and overlay exports share this new polygon. Zero RGBA outside ownership. Gallery patches decode exported PNG bytes and assemble ground then overlays using ordinary image.Draw Over at integer runtime cell translations, at BOTH 2x and 4x. They do not rerender world geometry or conceal sprite assembly gaps.",
  "path_interior": "Path-only organic interior. Let S(t)=clamp(t,0,1)^2*(3-2*clamp(t,0,1)), E=S((minimum signed polygon-edge distance-8)/8), A=2pi(x/142+y/80), B=2pi(x/142-y/80), using world x/y. Warp local route lookup by E*(0.55*sin(A),0.55*sin(B)), displacement length \u003c=0.55*sqrt(2)*E world px. Wear=0.2*sin(5*A+2*B+0.7)*sin(3*B-A); core radius=width/2+E*(0.4*sin(A+0.4)*cos(B)+wear). For 3+-port junctions smoothly union core SDF with a central disc of radius 0.65*width at warped coordinates: h=max(1.5-abs(core-disc),0)/1.5, merged=min(core,disc)-1.5*h*h/4, core=core+E*(merged-core). Border=border*(1-0.45*E+0.25*E*sin(B+0.7)). Pocket=S((sin(2*A+0.3)*cos(3*B-0.4)+0.15)/0.9); bank opacity=1-0.75*E*pocket; final alpha=outer_AA*(core_AA+(1-core_AA)*bank_opacity). The 8-world-pixel edge zone is unchanged; full variation begins at 16 px. Cores stay opaque; irregular translucent earth verges reveal underlying terrain without baked-in grass. Road and stream arithmetic is unchanged.",
  "path_profile": "Unmarked fine compacted earth core nominal width7worldpx with earth border0.75worldpx per side, protected eight-world-pixel contacts. Organic interior course/width/edge wear, rounded confluences, translucent earth fringe reveals underlying ground; narrower and warmer than14worldpx gravel roads.",
  "previous_acceptance": {
    "scope": "Historical source set before the current redraw; not an approval of the current artwork.",
